#: f171b2dfafa9453287181f2fd36b6189
msgid ""
"**Goal**: walk each `<load>` child in the pre-load, common, and post-load"
" configuration nodes and `dlopen` the matching DSO. Attribute semantics "
"and the two `modules.conf` files: [Architecture](01-architecture.md"
"#runtime-load-tag)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:155
#: c3608c82c1db4343a5b0e27e95e37d2a
msgid ""
"**Find the configuration node.** `switch_xml_open_cfg(\"modules.conf\", "
"&cfg, NULL)` (`cf` in `switch_loadable_module_init`). The same helper is "
"used with `\"pre_load_modules.conf\"` and `\"post_load_modules.conf\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:156
#: 9589e1438f0b44db9375e1d0c0e2b595
msgid ""
"**Iterate `<load>`.** `switch_xml_child(cfg, \"modules\")` then "
"`switch_xml_child(mods, \"load\")`. Document-commented tags are not "
"children. Empty `module` or a dotted name that is not a known DSO suffix "
"is skipped (`Invalid extension for …`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:157
#: a17936c62f134b7d8d414974621c1cc6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Open and call load.** Path `{dir}/{module}.so` (non-Windows). "
"`switch_loadable_module_load_file` resolves `{filename}_module_interface`"
" and invokes `load_func_ptr(&module_interface, pool)`. For Sofia that is "
"`mod_sofia_load()`, which registers the endpoint and runs "
"`config_sofia(SOFIA_CONFIG_LOAD, NULL)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:158
#: 254695316c0348ed8f1bdf6b60b34930
msgid ""
"**After the lists.** `switch_loadable_module_runtime()` starts each "
"module’s optional runtime thread. If every XML list was empty, the loader"
" loads all files in `mod_dir` instead (`No modules loaded, assuming 'load"
" all'`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:160
#: f5865ada683e41a6ba3b677e78e20ac3
msgid ""
"`reloadxml` replaces the XML root; it does **not** re-execute these "
"`<load>` rows. Use `load` / `unload` / `reload` (or restart) to change "
"the set of DSOs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:164
#: 8abfa4458a334fe68fa0088de0583ca4
msgid "Interface registry lookup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:168
#: 8614aa266b0048869987882791f5624d
msgid ""
"**Trigger**: a **name** appears at runtime — dialplan "
"`application=\"bridge\"`, ESL/`fs_cli` `api status`, originate `sofia/…`,"
" or a codec IANA name. The module that implements that name has already "
"run its load function during startup ([Runtime load tag](#runtime-load-"
"tag))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:169
#: 741cc8ddd2f64c8ca7fbb4db6c21f21b
msgid ""
"**Goal**: resolve the string through `loadable_modules.*_hash` to a "
"function pointer and invoke it. Architecture and why this is not an IDL: "
"[Loadable module contract](01-architecture.md#loadable-module-contract)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:195
#: f7b730e720eb4fde9468932d74e3a1a5
msgid ""
"**Register at load.** `SWITCH_ADD_APP(app_interface, \"bridge\", …, "
"audio_bridge_function, …)` in `mod_dptools.c` appends a "
"`switch_application_interface_t` on the module bag. `SWITCH_ADD_API(..., "
"\"status\", …, status_function, …)` in `mod_commands.c`. Sofia has no "
"`SWITCH_ADD_ENDPOINT`; it `create_interface(..., "
"SWITCH_ENDPOINT_INTERFACE)` and sets `interface_name = \"sofia\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:196
#: 7bc79f4a84ce48119af806c69ba11afd
msgid ""
"**Index.** `switch_loadable_module_process` inserts each named node into "
"`application_hash` / `api_hash` / `endpoint_hash` (and logs `Adding "
"Application 'bridge'`). Duplicate names last-writer-wins at hash insert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:197
#: 65523e33597e4fd49381face43657a5f
msgid ""
"**Application dispatch.** `mod_dialplan_xml` `exec_app` / "
"`switch_core_session_execute_application` → "
"`switch_loadable_module_get_application_interface(app)` → "
"`switch_core_session_exec` → "
"`application_interface->application_function(session, arg)`. `bridge`’s "
"function may later call `switch_ivr_multi_threaded_bridge`; that is an "
"implementation detail, not the registry key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:198
#: 63731b64bcce48699f23c4ed6e2c9a0c
msgid ""
"**API dispatch.** `switch_api_execute(cmd, arg, session, stream)` → "
"`get_api_interface(cmd)` → `api->function`. Used by console, ESL "
"`api`/`bgapi`, and other modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:199
#: 298f772a799549f7baecd94b8956502a
msgid ""
"**Endpoint dispatch.** `switch_core_session_outgoing_channel(..., "
"\"sofia\", profile, …)` → `get_endpoint_interface` → "
"`io_routines->outgoing_channel`. Inbound Sofia sessions attach the same "
"endpoint interface when the session is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:201
#: 85323dc293cf4beb9257d947d6560980
msgid "Worked example: `answer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:203
#: 31d2dcebbcc64a5d9fff411f6ba8da96
msgid ""
"The shortest real chain from XML to C. Source: `mod_dptools.c` "
"(`SWITCH_MODULE_DEFINITION(mod_dptools, mod_dptools_load, "
"mod_dptools_shutdown, NULL)`), `switch_loadable_module.h` "
"(`SWITCH_ADD_APP`), `switch_core_session.c`, "
"`switch_core_state_machine.c` `switch_core_standard_on_execute`. Macro "
"field names: the name is **`interface_name`**, not `application_name`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:226
#: 501dad5e5b074363982544f8cfef5663
msgid ""
"**Load (once).** `mod_dptools_load` calls "
"`switch_loadable_module_create_module_interface`, then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:233
#: 967f1556506643da916125c0f66358ee
msgid ""
"That expands to `create_interface(..., SWITCH_APPLICATION_INTERFACE)` and"
" fills `interface_name`, `application_function`, descriptions, "
"`syntax=\"\"`, `flags`. `process()` inserts `\"answer\"` into "
"`application_hash`. `answer_function` is `SWITCH_STANDARD_APP`: `static "
"void (session, data)` ending in `switch_channel_answer`. Flags "
"`SAF_SUPPORT_NOMEDIA` skip the “needs media / pre_answer” path in "
"`execute_application_get_flags`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:235
#: 3f66a7f32d9f4281909e6c3e9115e048
msgid ""
"**Hunt (per call).** `<action application=\"answer\"/>` does not `dlopen`"
" anything. `mod_dialplan_xml` queues the string `\"answer\"` on the "
"caller extension (or `exec_app` if inline). The consumer never mentions "
"`mod_dptools`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:237
#: 9723178570844a1dbbd7b8c5ccf25017
msgid ""
"**Execute.** `switch_core_session_execute_application` is `#define` → "
"`switch_core_session_execute_application_get_flags`. Lookup failure: "
"`Invalid Application` + hangup `DESTINATION_OUT_OF_ORDER`. Success: "
"`switch_core_session_exec` → pointer call. Log line `EXECUTE [depth=…] … "
"answer()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/05-workflows.md:239
#: 90dd7cbd169e44dbabfe653f7226181c
msgid ""
"Same pattern for API `\"status\"` via `SWITCH_ADD_API` / "
"`switch_api_execute`. Endpoints differ: name → **vtable** "
"(`io_routines`), not one function. See the "
"[Architecture](01-architecture.md) page for the golden path."
msgstr ""

